{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>Rise early in the morning, etc.</b> He was charged with three commandments: (1) that he go with alacrity (בהשכמה); (2) that he present himself before him — meaning, that he not bow his head and not stoop his stature in the manner of those who stand before great men, but rather like a great man standing before a small one, for the Master had already made him a lord and ruler over him. And he needed to be commanded to this because by his natural disposition Moses tended to bow his head somewhat in the manner of the humble; therefore He said that before Pharaoh he is not to conduct himself thus. He further hinted to him that this particular detail of saying to him ״present yourself״ — he is not to remove from himself his accustomed humility in every place, but only before Pharaoh; but in his heart let him be humble and lowly before El Elyon, while his body stands erect and his heart is humbled by the awe of Him whose glory fills all the earth. And the third commandment: ״ואמרת אליו״ — and so forth."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:26:03.876695570Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}